  "major_resolutions": [
    "Moby Dick retains air-cooled cylinders with water-cooled heads; its fan architecture is a distinct branch, with exact fan specification still unverified.",
    "K3 air-to-air change concerns charge cooling, not head-water conversion.",
    "2003 replica proposal was abandoned; proposed 11000 rpm/3500 cfm/15 hp not treated as test data.",
    "EB reported power points remain replica-specific, with no full curve or uncertainty.",
    "FSH 1.50 kg and StuttGear 1.60 kg are item/set masses, not bare-rotor measurements.",
    "Torres 7075 CNC rotor and FSH cast-aluminium wheel are different products, not one factory alloy specification.",
    "Nine-blade carbon-fibre fan belongs to Group C source context, not the 1976 Group 5 car.",
    "Source-local adoption flags are not automatic simulation admission; whole-engine calibration remains incomplete."
  ],
